\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L1VTQV9GYWN1bHR5X0RldmVsb3BtZW50X0dyYW50XzI1S19GdWxsX1Byb3Bvc2FsXzIwMjQtMS5wZGY%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=156286163&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=s1xws%2BxJRW8n5YyI7zHAnKxTU8w%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 USA_Faculty_Development_Grant_25K_Full_Proposal_2024-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L0NsYXJrIFJTREcgMjAyNSBhd2FyZCBsZXR0ZXItMS5wZGY%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=156286163&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=ao%2FzjGpIhgfR6USrFQxkP08L5vM%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 Clark RSDG 2025 award letter-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f43\fs16\cf20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li0\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Clark, G. W., "An Investigation of Cyberattacks on Edge AI Components of Self-Driving Vehicles," Sponsored by NSF 2023 Seed Awards for Researchers at Junior Level (SARJ), Internal to the University, $15,000.00. (February 1, 2024 - January 31, 2025).}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Self-driving vehicles are becoming increasingly popular, but they are also susceptible to cybersecurity attacks. These attacks can target the hardware, firmware/operating system, and application layers of the vehicle, as well as the machine learning model.}\line \line {\fs20 A relatively new architecture for autonomous driving is the end-to-end system. In this system, sensor inputs are directly connected to a deep learning neural network, which controls the steering, braking, and acceleration of the vehicle. End-to-end systems can be trained using imitation learning or reinforcement}\line {\fs20 learning. While reinforcement learning is more efficient, it is also more susceptible to cyberattacks.}\line \line {\fs20 The goal of this research is to develop a self-driving vehicle that uses an end-to-end system architecture}\line {\fs20 as an Edge AI test platform for cybersecurity research. This research will help to identify and mitigate the}\line {\fs20 security challenges posed by end-to-end autonomous driving systems.}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L1NBUkpfTlNGX0dyYW50LTMtMS5wZGY%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=146415126&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=N5dIHBDDBze3kh8EENLCrVTDWgw%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 SARJ_NSF_Grant-3-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L1NBUkogQXdhcmQgRW1haWwtMS5wZGY%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=146415126&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=53ZlzvyI9n%2BMZ41T%2Fmi6Ra8PA7Y%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 SARJ Award Email-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f43\fs16\cf20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li0\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Clark, G. W., "A Comparison of Invasive vs. Non-Invasive Side-Channel Analysis Attacks," Sponsored by Faculty Development Grant Council Program, Internal to the University, $5,000.00. (January 1, 2023 - December 31, 2023).}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Cyber-physical systems are susceptible to side-channel analysis (SCA) attacks during the cryp- tosystem process [1]. Using Di\u8629 erential Power Analysis (DPA), Electromagnetic (EM) radiation, and other SCA attacks, adversaries can correlate physical elements such as power usage and current flow to determine the bit pattern of a secret crypto key during the decryption process.}\line {\fs20 Previous research at the University of South Alabama has examined SCA vulnerabilities and their defense by analyzing EM radiation leakage of an integrated circuit (IC) with success [2]. This research will go further by removing the physical cover of a microprocessor to gain access to the integrated circuits on its silicon wafer. The removal of this barrier will lead to improved analysis and open new areas of research such as fault injection attacks of an IC via laser. The project will require purchasing a high-power laboratory microscope.}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L1VTQV9GREdfR2VvcmdlQ2xhcmstMS5wZGY%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=124798482&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=H5JrkqWJ8OY01bU1WJJRcnfXPz8%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 USA_FDG_GeorgeClark-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L0F3YXJkIE5vdGlmaWNhdGlvbi0xLnBkZg%3D%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=124798482&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=ApkMkKXTnSbk%2BhqmkNL0JCxthOE%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 Award Notification-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f43\fs16\cf20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li360\ri0\widctlpar\keepn\outlinelevel2 \b\f1\fs20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li720\ri0\widctlpar\keepn\outlinelevel2 \b\f1\fs20{Currently Under Review}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li0\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Clark, G. W., "CAREER," Sponsored by National Science Foundattion, External to the University, $472,228.00. (2026 - Present).}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Current methods of classification using neural networks are susceptible to adversarial attacks. Neural}\line {\fs20 networks can be misled by these attacks because they are trained on large datasets that can generalize poorly}\line {\fs20 on unseen data. Attackers exploit this vulnerability by crafting adversarial samples consisting of undetectable}\line {\fs20 perturbations to the input data. In the real world, these attacks can have serious consequences, such as}\line {\fs20 an autonomous vehicle misinterpreting a stop sign. Research on defense against these attacks focuses on}\line {\fs20 adversarial training, where AI models are trained on benign and adversarial samples. However, training AI}\line {\fs20 models on every possible adversarial sample is time consuming and unrealistic. Ideally, robot systems should}\line {\fs20 be able to detect adversarial attacks on their AI models in real-time to prevent potentially dire outcomes.}\line {\fs20 The project will proceed in four thrusts:}\line {\fs20 \bullet  Thrust 1 will involve establishing robotic simulation and physical testbeds for adversarial attacks and}\line {\fs20 developing adversarial threat models that target the testbed robots\rquote  perception system.}\line {\fs20 \bullet  Thrust 2 will entail collecting side-channel data (e.g. power traces, timing data) under normal and}\line {\fs20 adversarial conditions. Data preprocessing and validation will also be performed in this thrust.}\line {\fs20 \bullet  Thrust 3 will encompass reconstructing the robot\rquote s system dynamics by creating and analyzing phase}\line {\fs20 space graphs to identify normal behavior from adversarial behavior.}\line {\fs20 \bullet  Thrust 4 will integrate the detection system into a functional prototype via a commercial edge device that}\line {\fs20 will attach to an existing robot enabling passive monitoring of the onboard AI system without modifying}\line {\fs20 its internal software.}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L05TRl9DQVJFRVJfR3JhbnRfUHJvcG9zYWxfMjAyNV9HVF9UZW1wbGF0ZS0xLnBkZg%3D%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=176417004&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=05Sh9T7bWmzx0TfMMuC4OKH%2F%2BW4%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 NSF_CAREER_Grant_Proposal_2025_GT_Template-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f43\fs16\cf20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li360\ri0\widctlpar\keepn\outlinelevel2 \b\f1\fs20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li720\ri0\widctlpar\keepn\outlinelevel2 \b\f1\fs20{Not Funded}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li0\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Clark, G. W., "Robot Path Planning Algorithms using a Digital Twin," Sponsored by Research and Scholarly Development Grant Proposal 2023, Internal to the University, $25,000.00. (January 1, 2024 - December 31, 2024).}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Robots, such as autonomous vehicles, are increasingly operating in collaborative environments with human beings. Given the risk posed by these large autonomous robots, the algorithms and machine learning models used for path planning must be both accurate and efficient. The objective of this research will be to compare}\line {\fs20 traditional path planning algorithms Hybrid A* and D* Lite (pronounced Hybrid A star and D star Lite) along with the Proximal Policy Optimization algorithm which employs reinforcement learning using neural networks. The research will be conducted in two phases.}\line \line {\fs20 In phase 1 of this research, a simulation environment will be created for comparing the path planning methods. In this phase, a virtual model or digital twin will be created that accurately represents Shelby Hall. The digital twin and a virtual model of the Jackal robot will be loaded onto the Unity 3D simulation platform. The three path planning methods will be implemented, evaluated, and compared in the simulation environment. In phase 2 the implementation and training data from the simulation will be transferred to a physical Jackal robot for use in the actual Shelby Hall. The path planning methods will again be evaluated and compared with the evaluation results obtained from the virtual environment.}\line \line {\fs20 The data and results collected from this research will provide insight into which path planning algorithm is more accurate and more efficient. Additionally, the development of the digital twin, simulation environment, and Jackal robot artifacts will be useful in future robotics research conducted in the School of Computing.}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=Z2Vvcmdld2NsYXJrL2NvbmdyYW50L1VTQV9GYWN1bHR5X0RldmVsb3BtZW50X0dyYW50XzI1S19GdWxsX1Byb3Bvc2FsLTItMS5wZGY%3D&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=146415190&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=bfMga9v2j0Ie39FlR3JFzC51F%2Fk%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 USA_Faculty_Development_Grant_25K_Full_Proposal-2-1.pdf}}}}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f43\fs16\cf20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi0\li0\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{Benton, R. G. (Principal), Andel, T. R. (Co-Principal), Black, M. E. (Supporting), Borchert, G. M. (Supporting), Bourrie, D. M. (Supporting), Chow, A. (Supporting), Clark, G. W. (Co-Principal), Davidson, C. C. (Supporting), Green, R. E. (Supporting), Johnsten, T. (Supporting), Langley, R. (Supporting), McDonald, J. T. (Supporting), Russ, S. H. (Co-Principal), Shaban, M. (Supporting), Benton, G. (Co-Principal), "MRI Internal Competition: Development of FPGA/GPU Cluster for Machine Learning and Cyber-Security Algorithms (002879)," Sponsored by Research and Economic Development, University of South Alabama, Internal to the University, $807,041.00. (February 21, 2023).}\par
\pard\plain\s0\ql\fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20{The goal of this application was to compete in an internal competition; the competition was designed to select which ideas could be submitted to the NSF Major Research Instrumentation grant for February 2023.  The idea that was submitted by this group was to develop a GPU and FPGA enabled Machine Learning and Cyber-Security Cluster. The two fields have been slowly incorporating the other perspective to achieve more robust solutions, although they obviously have applications independent of each other. Cyber-Security have been incorporating Machine Learning methodologies to detect malware, discover potential compromises and to detect zero-day challenges. At the same time, security of the ML systems are becoming an increasing topic of focus, as the ML pipeline has multiple points of attack, which can compromise the value and effectiveness of the ML operation.}\par
\pard\plain\s36\ql\fi0\li1080\ri0\widctlpar \f1\fs20\cf2\ul{}{\field{\*\fldinst { HYPERLINK "https://www.digitalmeasures.com/login/southalabama/sso/survey/ui/showFile?file=cmJlbnRvbi9jb25ncmFudC9NUkkgMjAyMl8yMDIzIExPSV9VcGRhdGVkLTEucGRm&surId=18285729&nodeId=140178&sdId=125308028&sdSurId=18285729&rptId=1676&ver=2&sgntr=viyXwL%2BmX3rQnchbKCQbOUhiscE%3D" }}{\fldrslt {{\fs20 MRI 2022_2023 LOI_Updated-1.pdf}}}}\par
